WEBVTT

00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:04.760
ADDIE is often drawn as a sequence, but effective eLearning teams use it iteratively.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.815
New information appears during analysis, design, development, implementation,

00:00:08.815 --> 00:00:09.760
and evaluation.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.360
A subject matter expert may identify missing nuance.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.460
A prototype may reveal confusing flow.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.030
A pilot may expose assumptions about learner context.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.910
Evaluation may show that the course needs maintenance.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.630
Review checkpoints keep iteration controlled.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:24.680
Analysis review confirms the problem and audience.

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.979
Design review confirms objectives, structure, practice, and assessment.

00:00:27.979 --> 00:00:32.400
Development review checks accuracy, usability, accessibility, and technical behavior.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.515
Implementation review checks launch readiness.

00:00:34.515 --> 00:00:36.910
Evaluation review turns results into decisions.

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.520
These checkpoints prevent late surprises from becoming uncontrolled redesign.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.315
Change control is especially important after launch.

00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:44.295
Content ages.

00:00:44.295 --> 00:00:45.715
Compliance requirements change.

00:00:45.715 --> 00:00:47.195
Product screens update.

00:00:47.195 --> 00:00:48.200
Policies are revised.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.550
Learner feedback identifies unclear sections.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.090
Without revision logs, version history, and ownership,

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.690
a course can become inaccurate while still appearing polished.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:58.380
A maintainable course has a clear path for updates.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.385
Not every issue should be fixed immediately.

00:01:00.385 --> 00:01:04.070
Some changes are critical because they affect accuracy, compliance, accessibility,

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:06.275
or learner ability to complete the course.

00:01:06.275 --> 00:01:09.275
Other improvements can be backlogged for the next scheduled update.

00:01:09.275 --> 00:01:12.520
Good change control helps the team decide what to fix now, what to monitor,

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.960
and what to defer.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:16.075
Iteration is not a sign the original design failed.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:17.720
It is how courses stay useful.

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:20.636
The workplace changes, learners change, and evidence accumulates.

00:01:20.636 --> 00:01:24.900
ADDIE gives teams a way to update learning intentionally instead of reacting to every

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:26.720
request as a separate emergency.
